/-!
# The minorant of the `ℓ = 9/25` window certificate as a function, and its exact moments

The symbol minorant `m` of the first prime-visible window certificate (`T = 25`) is piecewise
polynomial, built (GPP-bridge `work/claude-code/rung1/b_exact_mirror.py`) from the exact local
lower bound of the elementary function `G_80 ≤ Ψ₂ - β₂(25)` (`GppWindowGM.GM_le`), minus its error
bound: on `(i/4, (i+1)/4]`, `i < 100`, it is the polynomial with ascending coefficients
`pieceTable[i]`, and `m(r) = m(|r|)`. This file defines it (`mfun`) and proves, for every `s`,

  `∫_{-25}^{25} m(r) r^s dr = momTable[s]`   (`integral_mfun_mul_pow`, `s < 96`),

the moment table being generated and then checked here by `decide +kernel` against the exact
piecewise formula. That is what turns the spectral entries of the window form into rational
arithmetic (`GppWindowEntries.abs_spec_sub_moments_le`).

**What is not here:** the validity `m ≤ Ψ₂ - β₂(25)` on `[-25, 25]` and the bound `|m| ≤ M`. That is
input (b) of the certificate, a separate file. Unconditional; no `sorry`, no axioms.
-/

